Z||000000||bilbo||05-21-2001||11:12 PM||||I'm going to be changing plugs and wires this week and I was thinking of splitfire on both anybody done this and had any problems with performance? Also underdrive pulley from fiero store says 6% increase in hp anybody done this and can you feel a difference in power delivery??  Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||05-21-2001||11:40 PM||||my $0.02<P>DON'T do it, I throw so many away because they foul up fast. Unless you like cleaning plugs constantly . . . . . .  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Scott||05-21-2001||11:51 PM||||Don't waste your money on Splitfires, they're  not worth it.  They don't offer a noticable difference in performance IMHO (and I've tried them in a HO V-8 car and a sport bike).  Electricity will always take the path of least resistance, meaning that which ever prong is closest to the electrode will be the one that sparks; therefore, they don't offer an improvement over normal plugs.<BR>Scott<BR> ||||reg||4
Z||000003||sjp777||05-22-2001||12:38 AM||||the power pulley however is worth every penny and the 6% is a pretty fair assessment<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
